  "solution": {
    "text": "Conductivity changes with the concentration of electrolyte. The number of ions per unit volume carrying the current decreases on dilution, so conductivity (K) always decreases with decrease in concentration.<br />Molar. Conductivity increases with dilution.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munder><msub><mo>&#8743;</mo><mtext>m</mtext></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>molar</mtext><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mtext>conductivity</mtext></mrow></mfenced></munder><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mtext>K</mtext></mrow><mtext>C</mtext></mfrac></math>"
  }
